{
  "requirement": "Bedrock configurations MAY supply `credentials` containing nonempty\n`access_key_id`, `secret_access_key`, and optional nonempty `session_token`.\nOllama configurations MAY supply a nonempty `api_key`. Habeas MUST reject a\nBedrock record combining explicit credentials with `aws_profile`, and an Ollama\nrecord combining `api_key` with `api_key_env`.\n\nExplicit credentials MUST be passed directly to the selected provider without\nchanging process environment variables or writing credential files. Saved\nexplicit values MUST round-trip; credentials resolved from profiles or the\nenvironment MUST NOT be serialized back. Debug output, configuration diagnostics,\nusage records, and initial prompts MUST NOT include credential values. TOML\ndiagnostics MUST NOT echo credential-containing source lines. An active workspace\nfile containing explicit credentials MUST be excluded from model source reads by\ndefault under {cite}`requirements.authoring.source_tools`; explicit workspace path\noverrides still apply.\n\nDocumentation MUST discourage literal credentials in workspace files and\nrecommend AWS profiles or environment-variable references. Examples MUST use\nplaceholders and explain that workspace files may be committed or read as source\nwhen explicitly allowed.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: `requirements.authoring.credentials` is met.** The implementation is complete and marked, and the tests cover the main cases and failure paths. I did not run the tests; this is from reading the code and the tests.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- **Nonempty values and mutual exclusion.** `BackendConfig::validate` (`src/config.rs`, marked `{impl}`) covers each rule.\n  - It rejects Bedrock `credentials` combined with `aws_profile`.\n  - It rejects Ollama `api_key` combined with `api_key_env`.\n  - It rejects empty `access_key_id`, `secret_access_key`, optional `session_token`, and empty `api_key`.\n  - `UserConfig::parse` and `WorkspaceConfig::parse` both call it.\n- **Direct pass-through.**\n  - `bedrock_sdk_loader` in `src/authoring/providers.rs` builds an in-memory `Credentials` value and calls `credentials_provider(...)`. It touches no environment variables and writes no files.\n  - `RigProvider::connect` passes the Ollama key with `with_api_key`, resolved through `OllamaConfig::api_key` and `api_key_from`.\n- **Round-trip and no write-back of resolved values.**\n  - `SecretString` serializes transparently, so literal values survive a save and reload.\n  - An `api_key_env` reference serializes as the variable name only. The resolved value is never stored.\n  - Profiles are stored only as the profile name.\n- **No credential values in output.**\n  - `SecretString`'s `Debug` prints `<redacted>`, and every config type derives `Debug` through it.\n  - The usage record is content-free by design.\n  - The initial prompt is built from mandatory inputs, and the credential-bearing workspace file is excluded from those.\n- **TOML diagnostics.** `parse_document` reports only \"invalid TOML syntax at line/column\". `decode` calls `error.set_input(None)` and replaces every value found under `credentials` or `api_key` with `<redacted>`, using `credential_values` to collect them.\n- **Workspace-file exclusion.**\n  - `load_workspace_evidence` sets `contains_credentials` when any config has `credentials` or `api_key`.\n  - `PathPolicy::load` stores that file as `credential_file`.\n  - `SourceAccess::path` denies it before the default rules, but only after the explicit allow check, so an explicit allow still overrides.\n  - It matches the requested path, the resolved target, and the canonicalized path, so symlink aliases are covered.\n  - Every tool (`habeas`, `list_files`, `outline`, `ripgrep`, `references`) goes through `path` or `file`.\n  - The tool descriptions in `definitions()` say the file is excluded.\n- **Documentation.**\n  - `md/requirements/authoring.md` (\"Editing the file\") calls literal credentials supported but not recommended, and warns that a workspace file may be committed.\n  - It states that an explicit allow exposes the file to the model and records it as evidence inputs.\n  - It gives a placeholder-only example, and a test asserts those values are uppercase placeholders.\n  - `md/reference.md` prefers profiles and environment references, and links to the credential examples.\n  - Both sections carry `{impl}` markers.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **`tests/configuration.rs`, `explicit_credentials_round_trip_but_diagnostics_and_debug_redact_them`.**\n  - It checks Debug redaction and the TOML round-trip.\n  - It checks that malformed credential inputs, including a wrong type, trailing garbage, and a non-table `credentials`, produce errors without the secret.\n  - It checks each rejection rule: `aws_profile` conflict, `api_key_env` conflict, and the three empty-value cases.\n- **`ollama_authentication_resolves_separately_and_rejects_missing_values`.** A missing or empty environment variable is an error, and the resolved value is not serialized.\n- **`evidence_configuration_ignores_unused_authoring_settings_and_detects_credentials`.** Credential detection works, and errors don't echo the value.\n- **`src/authoring/access.rs`, `workspace_credentials_are_excluded_unless_explicitly_allowed`.** The file is denied by default, the error text has no secret, and an explicit allow permits it.\n- **`src/authoring/providers.rs`, `explicit_bedrock_credentials_reach_the_sdk_without_the_default_chain`.** The access key, secret key, session token, and region reach the SDK.\n- **`tests/authoring_cli.rs`, `authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file`.** End to end, the literal key is sent as the Ollama credential. It does not appear in the request body (prompt), usage record, stdout, or stderr.\n- **`missing_or_empty_api_key_env_fails_before_any_model_request`.** The failure happens before any model request.\n- **`tests/configuration.rs`, `documented_configuration_examples_are_complete_valid_files`.** It enforces that the one literal-credential example uses placeholders and that the documented TOML parses.\n\n## Residual observations\n\nNone of these is a requirement gap.\n\n- Exclusion of the credential file through `ripgrep` and `list_files` is tested only indirectly, through the shared `SourceAccess::path` check. The direct `file()` read is what the unit test covers.\n- A few thin helpers carry no `{impl}` marker for this requirement. `load_workspace_config` is one. They only delegate to the marked `decode`, and the tests exercise the redaction through them.",
